# decomposer's virtual cameras: make them cameras from the moment they exist.
#
# With exclusive_caps=1 a v4l2loopback device reports OUTPUT until a producer
# is streaming, and CAPTURE only after. PipeWire inspects a V4L2 device once,
# when udev announces it, and creates a camera source only if the device can
# capture at that moment. The module loads at boot, long before decomposer
# publishes a frame, so PipeWire records two output-only devices and never
# looks again: Chrome, Zoom's web client and every other application that
# takes its cameras from PipeWire never see them.
#
# v4l2loopback's keep_format control makes a device report CAPTURE whether or
# not a producer is attached. This rule sets a format and that control as each
# device appears. The format and the control must be set in one v4l2-ctl call:
# without keep_format the driver forgets the format when the setter closes.
# The engine re-pins its real format when it attaches.
#
# THE FILENAME NUMBER MATTERS, and so does PROGRAM (not RUN). PROGRAM executes
# while the rules are processed, which is before 60-persistent-v4l.rules runs
# v4l_id (so udev also records the device as a capture device) and before the
# event reaches listeners such as PipeWire.
#
# Devices are matched by name, not number, so a changed video_nr still works.
#
# Install:
#   sudo install -m 0644 packaging/59-decomposer-loopback.rules /etc/udev/rules.d/
#   sudo udevadm control --reload-rules
#   sudo modprobe -r v4l2loopback && sudo modprobe v4l2loopback
# (stop decomposer and close every application using either camera first)

ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="video4linux", ATTR{name}=="decomposer*", \
  PROGRAM="/usr/bin/v4l2-ctl -d $devnode --set-fmt-video-out=width=1920,height=1080,pixelformat=YU12 -c keep_format=1"
